 dated_source('src-ironkin-official-equality','Ironkin: equal mechanical partners','Games Workshop','https://www.warhammer-community.com/en-gb/articles/kYSZrSMB/lore-of-the-leagues-introducing-the-ironkin-mechanical-members-of-the-leagues/','Ironkin are Votann-created mechanical intellects integrated as equal partners; some work as Wayfinders.','Equal status does not by itself establish unconditional necessities or equal control of Ancestor Cores.',kind='official_reference',access='Indexed official intellect, equality and Wayfinder passages read'),
 dated_source('src-ths-fifthwave-cybershells','Fifth Wave: cybershell functions','Phil Masters and David Pulver / Steve Jackson Games','https://dokumen.pub/transhuman-space-classic-fifth-wave-1556344597.html','Bounded game-text passages describe common Fifth Wave cybershells with many functions and cyberdemocracy using AI to assist direct citizen power.','Indexed reproduced text, not a whole-book read; local rights and the difference between AI and teleoperation remain important.',kind='primary_text',access='Indexed cybershell and cyberdemocracy glossary passages read'),
 dated_source('src-traveller1248-viral-citizens','Traveller 1248: Bearers of the Flame, Viral citizens','Avenger Enterprises','https://files.spawningpool.net/docs/Vault2.0.-.TTRPG-Gamebooks/Traveller/03%20-%20Traveller%2C%20The%20New%20Era%20%28TNE%29/Avenger%20Enterprises/Traveller%20-%201248%20-%20Sourcebook%202%20-%20Bearers%20of%20the%20Flame.pdf','Bounded sourcebook passage: many Viral beings are hostile or regard humans as inferior, but some civilized areas accept Viral beings as citizens.','Indexed passage from the later 1248 milieu, not proof of one named universal Virus state or automatic benign government.',kind='primary_text',access='Indexed Viral-plague and citizenship passage read'),
