def add(cid,rid,name,work,media,period,pop,excluded,desc,values,bounds,bases,facts,assumptions,qualification,regime=3,zero=True,proxy=False,synthetic=False,extra=None,branch=None,continuity=None):
 refs=D['decisions'][cid]['source_ids']+(extra or [])
 r=guessed_record(cid,rid,name,work,name,media,continuity or 'Named game/edition and stated period only',period,pop,excluded,desc,values,bounds,bases,refs,regime,facts,assumptions,qualification,zero=zero,proxy=proxy,branch=branch)
 if synthetic:
  r['scope']['person_proxy_kind']='active_synthetic_persons';r['axis_interpretation']={'nonworking':'Active synthetic-person participation, not a literal human rate.','control':'Independence from organic owners; internal machine hierarchy is a separate issue.','literal_human_nonworking':None}
 records.append(r);return r

add('c0705','starbound-glitch-medieval-zero','Starbound (the Glitch medieval societies)','Starbound',['game'],'The continuing medieval simulation-pattern communities','Active synthetic-person Glitch residents','Agrarian roles and simulated social scripts remain work when useful or assigned; inactive machines are excluded.',
'''The Glitch repeat medieval social and agrarian roles after a fault in their simulation-development system. Their artificial embodiment does not erase farming, craft, trade or care. The guarantee best guess is weak because inherited roles and technological bodies do not establish a dependable common necessities floor. This zero variant concerns an intentionally constrained material and social pattern rather than biological humans enjoying robots’ output.

 Synthetic operation independent of current organic owners gives negative control weight, while inherited programming and local hierarchies limit internal agency. Independence is not equal machine ownership. The low nonworking scenario counts useful or assigned agrarian tasks, craft, service and care among active residents. Calling a task simulated does not make it leisure when persons must perform it. Bodies, inactive mechanisms and automated scenery are not extra nonworkers. The wide intervals preserve variation between communities and emancipated individuals without turning the recognizable continuing medieval order into an unverified universal post-work utopia.''',
(.65,-.9,.15),([-.5,.98],[-1,-.35],[0,.7]),('Constrained agrarian access gives no assumed secure universal floor.','Synthetic independence coexists with inherited scripts and local hierarchy.','Active residents retain agrarian, craft and caring roles even inside a social simulation.'),
['Artificial medieval Glitch communities repeat agrarian tasks after a simulation-development fault.'],['Their material access and participation are active-person proxy estimates.','Assigned social roles count as work rather than automatically leisure.'],'Retain the famous constrained robot society with real contribution visible.',regime=6,proxy=True,synthetic=True)

add('c0706','outerwilds-nomai-zero','Outer Wilds (the living Nomai civilization)','Outer Wilds',['game'],'The inhabited Nomai settlements before extinction','Living biological Nomai residents, an explicit alien-person proxy','Extinct Nomai, recorded messages and surviving equipment are excluded; later travelers are a different population.',
'''Nomai mining and technical investigation show living people supplying resources and solving collective problems. Advanced transport and engineered settlements provide a plausible labor-saving background without establishing that all necessities arrive independently of contribution. The guarantee best guess allows a partial communal floor, qualified by resource needs and local hazards. The record is explicitly the living society before extinction, not empty ruins populated by imagined nonworkers.

 Collaborative resident and research-group agency receives positive control weight, with leadership and unequal access left within a wide interval. A biological alien civilization does not become an AI government because its devices are sophisticated. The modest nonworking scenario counts mining, research, construction, maintenance, care and useful creation. The number of preserved messages and the speed of travel are not labor statistics. This zero variant preserves actual useful work alongside technical capacity, using a disclosed alien-person proxy rather than pretending the setting supplies a human employment census.''',
(.05,.65,.25),([-.8,.95],[0,1],[.02,.8]),('A partial communal floor is plausible but resources and hazards remain.','Collaborative biological resident agency is central, not external AI rule.','Living residents retain mining, research and care; ruins and messages are excluded.'),
['Nomai mining-site and investigation exchanges show resource and technical work.'],['Settlement support and ownership are contextual best guesses.','Only the pre-extinction living population defines participation.'],'Retain the recognizable technical civilization with its living period and useful work explicit.',proxy=True)

add('c0708','outerworlds-halcyon-zero','The Outer Worlds (Halcyon’s corporate economy)','The Outer Worlds',['game'],'The functioning corporate towns during the game','Awake living human Halcyon residents','Cryosleep and death are excluded from nonworking participation; the Board’s future cycling plan is not universal current policy.',
'''Halcyon’s corporate towns depend on actual workers while advanced equipment and mechanized capacity coexist with elite consumption. The guarantee best guess is very weak because access is tied to corporate standing and coercive labor. This zero variant treats technical substitution as a limited material comparison, not proof that core human production has already disappeared. A corporation’s productive wealth does not become every resident’s secure right to necessities.

 Human corporate ownership receives control near concentrated authority rather than an independent AI sovereign. The low nonworking scenario counts production, administration, services, repair, care and useful informal activity among awake living residents. The Board’s cryosleep-and-hard-labor branch does not turn sleeping workers into leisure citizens: sleeping intervals are excluded and assigned labor still counts. The chosen ordinary period is separate from that proposed or branch-specific arrangement. Broad bounds preserve local conditions without making the fate of one settlement a common constitutional law for the whole colony.''',
(.95,.02,.2),([.55,1],[0,.3],[.02,.7]),('Coercive corporate status and labor make ordinary access highly insecure.','Human corporate owners dominate productive authority.','Awake residents retain useful work; cryosleep is not leisure.'),
['Corporate towns use human workers.','The Board branch cycles workers through cryosleep and hard labor to preserve elite consumption.'],['Ordinary technical substitution is a limited zero-variant qualification.','The ordinary period and Board branch are not averaged as one current policy.'],'Retain the famous working corporate colony with no cryosleep-to-leisure inference.')

add('c0711','warhammer-craftworld-aeldari','Warhammer 40,000 (Craftworld Aeldari)','Warhammer 40,000',['tabletop'],'The functioning post-Fall craftworld communities','Living biological Craftworld Aeldari residents','Soulstones, inactive dead souls and wraith constructs are not silently counted as living leisure residents; craftworlds vary.',
'''Craftworld habitats combine self-contained biomes with resource supplies and psychoactive material craft. Bonesingers create wraithbone artifacts, while residents pursue martial and other Paths. The guarantee best guess allows a strong internal floor with less wage dependence, qualified by war, local variation and continued supply needs. It is a partial post-work interpretation of engineered support, not a claim that every craftworld has identical rights or unlimited abundance.

 Resident institutions and distributed personal skill receive positive control weight. Psychic production is a technological-functional comparison, while the Bonesinger’s useful craft still counts as work. The moderate nonworking scenario includes private practice and leisure but counts care, maintenance, public art, administration and defense where useful or assigned. Every Path is not automatically a job, and every voluntary vocation is not automatically leisure. Only living biological residents enter this proxy denominator. Stored souls and war constructs do not inflate the number of supported nonworkers.''',
(-.55,.65,.4),([-.95,.65],[0,1],[.05,.9]),('Engineered habitats support a strong internal floor, qualified by supply and war.','Resident institutions and personal productive skill provide substantial shared agency.','Useful Paths, craft and care count; private practice and inactive souls are distinct.'),
['Craftworlds have self-contained biomes and resource supplies.','Official lore describes martial and other Paths and Bonesinger wraithbone creation.'],['A strong internal material floor is a low-confidence interpretation.','Living residents are separate from stored souls and constructs.'],'Retain the famous engineered habitat society with craftworld variation and real voluntary work visible.',regime=2,zero=False,proxy=True,extra=['src-aeldari-official-pathcraft'])

necron=add('c0712','warhammer-necron-active-persons-zero','Warhammer 40,000 (conscious awakened Necron elites)','Warhammer 40,000',['tabletop'],'An awakened functioning dynastic order','Active conscious alien-derived Necron nobles and specialists','Mindless Warriors, dormant identities and empty chassis are excluded; this is an elite-person cohort rather than all dynastic units.',
'''Necron dynasties awaken unevenly, and official lore distinguishes mindless Warriors from nobles with continuing personalities. The selected population is the conscious active elite and specialist cohort. Its technological bodies and maintenance systems provide material continuation, but access and bodily integrity remain unequal. The guarantee best guess allows a partial elite floor, qualified by damage, hierarchy and resource dependence rather than extending it to every chassis.

 Concentrated alien-derived dynastic persons receive control near the non-AI elite reference point. Mechanical embodiment alone does not make an ancient biological person an unrelated AI sovereign. The low nonworking scenario counts governance, research, repair, coordination and useful care; private obsessions are not automatically public work. Dormancy and mindless automatic action do not create leisure people. This zero variant is deliberately narrower than the whole army, with broad bounds for unequal awareness and support. It does not count biotransference casualties or a long sleep as release from labor.''',
(.05,.03,.2),([-.8,.95],[-.7,.4],[.02,.8]),('Elite maintenance supports continuation but unequal damage and access limit guarantees.','Alien-derived dynastic persons are central despite mechanical bodies.','Conscious awake persons retain governing/technical work; mindless units and dormancy are excluded.'),
['Necron dynasties awaken unevenly with mechanical hierarchy.','Official lore distinguishes mindless Warriors and sophisticated nobles with personalities.'],['Only active conscious nobles and specialists form the proxy cohort.','Machine embodiment is not automatically unrelated AI rule.'],'Retain the famous machine-bodied dynasty with consciousness and elite coverage explicit.',proxy=True,extra=['src-necron-official-consciousness'])
